## Scope

This license covers the content of this repository as published here —
case write-ups, patterns, practices, playbooks, and protocol documents.

**Commercial use is explicitly permitted.** You may use Open PRAOP
materials in paid consulting, training, internal implementation, or
product work. If you publicly distribute a modified version of the
Open PRAOP materials themselves, that modified version must carry the
same CC BY-SA 4.0 license — improvements to the shared corpus stay
shared.

## What is NOT covered by this license

- **The "PRAOP" / "Open PRAOP" name and any associated logo or
  trademark.** CC BY-SA covers the content, not the brand. You may fork
  and adapt the material and describe your work as "based on Open
  PRAOP," but you may not represent your fork or derivative as the
  official Open PRAOP project, an official certification, or an
  official Open PRAOP-branded framework.
- **Raw / private evidence.** Internal logs, original transcripts, full
  customer or company records, and any other unredacted source material
  are never covered by this license, whether or not they're referenced
  by an accepted case. Only material actually published in this public
  repository, and marked as the redacted/public version, is licensed
  here.
- **Third-party material quoted or referenced by a case** (e.g. a
  linked Reddit post, paper, or screenshot from an External Case, per
  §16 of the protocol). Inclusion in a case write-up does not relicense
  that third-party content — it remains under whatever terms its
  original source carries.
- **Future software components.** If Open PRAOP later ships tooling
  (a CLI, a de-identification scanner, preflight/validation tools,
  etc.), those are expected to ship under a separate permissive license
  (Apache License 2.0 is the current plan, for its explicit patent
  grant) rather than under CC BY-SA — code and open-content licensing
  serve different purposes and shouldn't be forced under one license.

## Contributions

By submitting a contribution (a case, practice, playbook, or edit) for
inclusion in this repository, you represent that you have the right to
submit it, and you agree that, if accepted, it may be distributed under
CC BY-SA 4.0 on the same terms as the rest of this repository. You
retain the rights to your own original contribution; this is a license
grant to the project, not a transfer of ownership. See `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

This license does not constitute legal, compliance, or safety advice.
